Kekê Tehsîn jî hat.
 
Brother Tehsîn came too.

162
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:00,000
Kekê Îbrahîm jî hat.
 
Brother Îbrahîm came too.

163
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:05,000
Erê cema'et wekî we dî ye.
 
Yes folks, as you saw.

164
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:13,000
Xal Hişyar bila nîv se'etekê boro ne, bi daran ardê xwo ke
samût ke, ma'nê cût boş bûn.
 
Uncle Hishyar, let half an hour pass, fix the logs to the
ground, make it firm, meaning the plowing was abundant.

165
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:15,000
Selamun 'eleykum.
 
Peace be upon you.

166
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:17,000
Wele hela xol.
 
By God, hello uncle.

167
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:22,000
De piçkî çûçik binerin.
 
Look at the chicks a little bit.

168
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:26,000
Maşallah, xudê bixefilîne.
 
Mashallah, may God protect them.

169
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:30,000
Da cama... da dibê sibê da baran e.
 
The glass... it says tomorrow implies rain.

170
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:34,000
Vê me'nê xal Hişyar samût ke sekinî ye.
 
In this sense, Uncle Hishyar secure it, it is
stopped/stable.

171
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:54,000
Dikin... yekser bin ax kin... ma'nê cût ke.
 
They are doing it... bury it under soil immediately...
meaning plow it.

172
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:03,000
Erê cema'eta me ya hêja...
 
Yes, our dear group...

173
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:06,000
Em li hûfê Hecîka ne, Hecîkê Jêrin.
 
We are in the hollow of Hecîka, Lower Hecîka.

174
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:10,000
Zêdetir me wera bere gotibû gundê Mîskê ye.
 
Previously, we had told you it is Mîskê village.

175
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:13,000
Gundê Dêrîş jî li kû ye, ji me ve dûr e.
 
Where Dêrîş village is too, it is far from us.

176
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:16,000
Em dê nuke çin Hecîkê Jorîn.
 
We will now go to Upper Hecîka.

177
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:36,000
Bi me ra bin, em a Hecîkê Jorîn.
 
Stay with us, we are [going to] Upper Hecîka.

178
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:06,000
Erê cema'et.
 
Yes folks.

179
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:14,000
Ev o Hecîkê Jorîn e, em nuke di kevin Hecîkê Jor.
 
This is Upper Hecîka, we are now entering Upper Hecîka.

180
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:34,000
Gundekî pir bilind e.
 
A very high village.

181
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:41,000
Erê, hevalên me, ev o Hecîka ye, Hecîkê Jor.
 
Yes, our friends, this is Hecîka, Upper Hecîka.

182
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:45,000
We em lê, nuke berî vê a ew ê jêr bî, ev ê jor e.
 
And we are here, just before this was the lower one, this is
the upper one.

183
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:47,000
Dûrçêr me bigir...
 
My cameraman, capture it...

184
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:54,000
Kesê gundê xwe nedî ye, kesê zîkrayatê xwe hene, milona xora
lê seyr ken, tebî'eta vê gundî pir xweş e.
 
Those who haven't seen their village, those who have
memories, let them watch it on their phones, the nature of
this village is very nice.

185
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:56,000
Gundekî pir bilind e.
 
A very high village.

186
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:58,000
Hember me gundê Dêrîş e.
 
Opposite us is Dêrîş village.

187
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:00,000
Hevalê min li gundê Dêrîş bigir.
 
My friend, capture Dêrîş village.

188
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:03,000
Nîzîk bike.
 
Zoom in.

189
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:23,000
Jê hevalê me ra.
 
For our friend.

190
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:28,000
Ev dara jî mezin e.
 
This tree is also big.

191
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:48,000
Wek wê dara jêr e.
 
It is like that tree below.

192
00:13:57,000 --> 00:14:00,000
Ev o seh'a reîsî ye.
 
This is the main square.

193
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:10,000
Bilindahiya...
 
The height...

194
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:13,000
Erê hevalên me, ev o Hecîkê Jorîn e.
 
Yes our friends, this is Upper Hecîka.

195
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:19,000
Ev seh'a Hecîka ye, hef dara jî li vir heye, emrê vê darê jî
mezin e.
 
This is the square of Hecîka, this tree is also here, the
age of this tree is also great.

196
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:21,000
Me ra, dûrçêr me bigir...
 
For us, my cameraman capture it...

197
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:22,000
Li gund bigir...
 
Capture the village...

198
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:24,000
War darê jî me ra daxîne.
 
Capture the tree for us as well.

199
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:26,000
Gundekî pir xweş e.
 
A very nice village.

200
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:37,000
Bilind e.
 
It is high.

201
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:40,000
Rûniştinê bin vê darê pir xweş e.
 
Sitting under this tree is very nice.

202
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:42,000
Xuseten evînî.
 
Especially [for] love.

203
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:47,000
Nuke xuseten evînî rûniştinê xwe pir xweş e.
 
Now, especially for love, sitting here is very nice.

204
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:52,000
Maşallah, çi darek mezin e, cîkî çûkê jî ser çêkiriye me dî
ye.
 
Mashallah, what a big tree, they have built a small spot on
it too, I saw.

205
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:53,000
Cîkî çûkê jî hene.
 
There are small spots [on it] too.

206
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:55,000
Oho, li ko.
 
Oho, look there.

207
00:14:55,000 --> 00:15:07,000
Cîkî çûkê jî hene.
 
There are small spots too.

208
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:09,000
Gundekî pir xweş e.
 
A very nice village.

209
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:13,000
Wekî hat dîtin, xanîyê xwo kevin, kevir...
 
As it was seen, their old houses, stone...

210
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:17,000
Bes xanî nûjen kirine, qata diduyan li ser çekirine.
 
But they have renovated the houses, built a second floor on
top.

211
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:22,000
Li vê gundî camîk heye, liko jûr, hember me.
 
In this village there is a mosque, look up, opposite us.

212
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:39,000
Ev camiya haker çêkirin e.
 
This mosque is built of stone.

213
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:59,000
Ev mal no kêf kirine. No evînê xora têyê bin vir çayê
çêdikin, qehwê çêdikin.
 
These people have enjoyed themselves. The lovers make tea
for themselves under here, make coffee.

214
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:07,000
Wekî we dî ye, hevyana hember me gundê Dêrîş e.
 
As you saw, that side opposite us is Dêrîş village.

215
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:26,000
Em nuke nêzîkî sînorê Tirkiyê ne.
 
We are now close to the Turkish border.

216
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:30,000
Erê hevalên me, cew germ e ke, welle cew xweş e.
 
Yes our friends, the weather is warm though, by God the
weather is nice.

217
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:34,000
Ev o mentiqa me, maşallah mentiqa me pir xweş e, sehra ye
mentiqa.
 
This is our region, mashallah our region is very nice, the
region is scenic.

218
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:37,000
Gidar mera bixwinin, bilindî jî.
 
Look at the trees for us, and the height.

219
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:38,000
Selamun 'eleykum.
 
Peace be upon you.

220
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:39,000
'Eleykum selam ser çava.
 
And upon you peace, you are welcome.

221
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:41,000
Tu bi xêr hatî, baş î inşallah?
 
Welcome, are you well, God willing?

222
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,000
Xwedê te bihêle, baş î.
 
May God keep you, you are well.

223
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:44,000
Welle gundê we gundekî pir xweş e.
 
Wallah, your village is a very nice village.

224
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:45,000
Em bilind e, he?
 
It is high, eh?

225
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:49,000
Em bilindbûna gund e, mentiqa pir xweş xûya têt o no.
 
The height of the village, the region looks very nice you
know.

226
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:52,000
Kîbar e. Gundê we pir otin e xalo?
 
It is distinct. Is your village very populated uncle?

227
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:54,000
Wellehî... ê pir otin e, mal dida...
 
Wallah... yes it is very populated, giving houses...

228
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:57,000
Mal d'bûne. Ê me em pir nînin.
 
There were houses. Yes, us, we are not many.

229
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:58,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

230
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:01,000
Xwedê destê te ser we ra bigire, Xwedê emrê te dirêj bike.
 
May God place his hand over you, may God extend your life.

231
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:06,000
Gundê we em bêjin Hecîkê Jêr bîn, me got em hên Hecîkê Jor
zê xora teswîr kin.
 
Your village, let's say we were in Lower Hecîka, we said
let's come to Upper Hecîka to film it too.

232
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:08,000
Hecîkê Jor bilind e...
 
Upper Hecîka is high...

233
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:11,000
Belê, mewqi'ê wê xweş e, pir xweş e.
 
Yes, its location is nice, very nice.

234
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:13,000
Xuseten bivara wera hîn xweş e.
 
Especially with its surroundings/views, it is even nicer.

235
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:14,000
Pir kîbar e.
 
Very distinct.

236
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:16,000
Te got çi?
 
What did you say?

237
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:23,000
Min got kû derê dixwazî tu bin em ji we re bigirin. Serê
xûnîkê bikşîne, baxçeyê bikşîne, çi wek vîdyo hûn dixwazin.
 
I said wherever you want, we can film for you. Film the top
of the fountain, film the garden, whatever you want as
video.

238
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:24,000
Xwedê ji te razî be.
 
May God be pleased with you.

239
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:26,000
Xwedê we biparêze.
 
May God protect you.

240
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:28,000
Xwedê te razî be. Paş virdo mal hene ne?
 
May God be pleased with you. Are there houses back this way?

241
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:29,000
Ê.
 
Yes.

242
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:32,000
Mamê 'ezîz, ev dara temenê wê çend sal e?
 
Dear uncle, how old is this tree?

243
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:35,000
Kuda dizanim, bab û bapîrê me gotiye...
 
How should I know, our fathers and grandfathers said...

244
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:38,000
Em serê xwe hildidin, em dibînin her wisa ye.
 
We lift our heads [grow up], we see it just like this.

245
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:39,000
Yanî kevnar e.
 
Meaning it is ancient.

246
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:40,000
Kevnar e.
 
It is ancient.

247
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:43,000
Çend sal diçit teqdîren?
 
How many years does it go approximately?

248
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:47,000
Teqdîren... 350-400 sal.
 
Approximately... 350-400 years.

249
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:48,000
400 sal e?
 
It is 400 years old?

250
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:50,000
Ew berû ye yan...?
 
Is it an oak or...?

251
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:51,000
Ew berû ye.
 
It is an oak.

252
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:54,000
Berû ye, belê berûya reş e?
 
It is an oak, but is it a black oak?

253
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:58,000
Berû du cûre hene, avî heye û bejî heye.
 
Oaks are two types, there is irrigated and there is
wild/dry-farmed.

254
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:00,000
Ev bejî ye yan avî ye?
 
Is this wild or irrigated?

255
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:02,000
Ev bejî ye.
 
This is wild.

256
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:05,000
Maşallah, bejî ye û ewqas mezin e.
 
Mashallah, it is wild and that big.

257
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:16,000
Ew avî... ew şikî ye jê.
 
The irrigated one... that is a branch/type of it.

258
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:19,000
Belê ev bejî ye, ev mekin e, ev jî demeke ne...
 
But this is wild, this is firm, this is also a time...

259
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:20,000
Berê wê heye?
 
Does it have fruit/acorns?

260
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:23,000
Berê wê îsal tine.
 
Its fruit is nonexistent this year.

261
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:25,000
Boçî îsal tine?
 
Why is it nonexistent this year?

262
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:28,000
Welleh, sal bo salê tê guhertin.
 
Wallah, it changes year to year.

263
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:33,000
Gelo dibêjin dara nêr heye û dara mê heye. Ev nêr e yan mê
ye?
 
They say there is a male tree and a female tree. Is this
male or female?

264
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:34,000
Ev mêk e.
 
This is a female.

265
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:36,000
Ev mê ye.
 
This is female.

266
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:37,000
Ê, nêr ber nakin.
 
Yes, males don't bear fruit.

267
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:44,000
Nêr ber nake, belê. Tenê nêr tov dide, tozkê dide.
 
Males don't bear fruit, yes. Males only give seed, give
pollen.

268
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:45,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

269
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:47,000
Zor spas xalê 'ezîz.
 
Many thanks dear uncle.

270
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:48,000
Ser çava.
 
You are welcome.

271
00:18:48,000 --> 00:19:08,000
Xwedê te bihêle.
 
May God keep you.

272
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:18,000
Erê cema'et, mişxolê xwe pirs kir.
 
Yes folks, we asked our questions.

273
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:21,000
Dibê 'emrê vê darê 350 sal, 400 sal e.
 
He says the age of this tree is 350 years, 400 years.

274
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:23,000
Bes ev dar a bejî ye.
 
But this tree is a wild one.

275
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:25,000
Dêrê jêr avî ye.
 
The [tree] below is irrigated.

276
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:29,000
Ew 'emrê jêr teqrîben hew jî 400 sal heye.
 
That age of the one below is approximately 400 years too.

277
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:33,000
Emrê xwe pir mezin e vê darê.
 
Its age is very great, this tree.

278
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:35,000
Mero bin em gundî din werin temam kin.
 
Let's go, let's complete [the tour of] the other village.

279
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:55,000
Bi me ra bin.
 
Stay with us.

280
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:59,000
Erê hevalên me, ev o gundê Hesen e, wer dibin.
 
Yes our friends, this is the village of Hesen, as they say.

281
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Kesê naskirî, gundê Hesen...
 
Those who know it, Hesen village...

282
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:05,000
Ev gundê Hesen e. Bes wellah hîna em neketine binof gundê
Hesen.
 
This is Hesen Village. But honestly, we haven't entered the
vicinity of Hesen Village yet.

283
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:06,000
Yanî rêka me hîn dûr e.
 
Meaning, our road is still far.

284
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:18,000
Ev gundê Hesen e. Mafreqê gundî jî li pêşiyê zotir... noko
li sêr kin.
 
This is Hesen Village. The intersection of the village is
further ahead... now watch it.

285
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:30,000
Maşalla vê kendalê bilind in. Mirov dikeve nava qulibandinê.
 
Mashallah, these cliffs are high. One feels like they are
rolling over.

286
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:49,000
Divero diherin gundê Hesen. Gundê Hesen dido dikeve qumraşê.
Ev rêka hîşta... gîb ev diro... qîr e.
 
From here, they go to Hesen Village. Hesen Village falls two
[ways/parts] towards Qumrash. This road is still... all the
way to here... is asphalt.

287
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:58,000
Ev o mafreqê gundê Hesen e.
 
This is the intersection of Hesen Village.

288
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:18,000
Havo gundê Hesen e.
 
There is Hesen Village.

289
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:25,000
Em nakin têkevinê, çîçik îş acele ye.
 
We won't enter it, the job is a bit urgent.

290
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:31,000
Yanî rêk pîşê me dûr e.
 
Meaning the road ahead of us is far.

291
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:36,000
Havo zûter divero diherin gundê Qada.
 
Here, sooner, from here we go to Qada Village.

292
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:39,000
Divero diherin gundê Qada û 'Amaro.
 
From here we go to Qada Village and Amaro.

293
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:59,000
Bi mar o bin. Noko emê werin gund jî derxin.
 
Stay with us. Now we will come and show the village too.

294
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:22,000
Xelkê maşalla kincê xwe şûştine, derkirine, hîşta dinê
germeke maşalla.
 
People, mashallah, have washed their clothes, put them out,
the world is still a bit warm, mashallah.

295
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:37,000
Kanî kincê xwe li şuwîn derdixin.
 
Look where they put their clothes out.

296
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:44,000
Maşalla, maşalla, evê dorê binêrin.
 
Mashallah, mashallah, look at this area.

297
00:22:44,000 --> 00:23:03,000
Maşalla çi şînkahîk e.
 
Mashallah, what greenery.

298
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:13,000
Cemaet wekî we dîye, maşalla gilek... bixwe ne wextê hîn zû
ye. Bes maşalla gilek paqij e, gilek biro germ e.
 
Folks, as you saw, mashallah very... actually it's not the
time, it's still early. But mashallah it's very clean, it's
very warm here.

299
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:21,000
Mêşê hingiv li ser pir in.
 
Honey bees are plentiful on it.

300
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:26,000
Yani hîn zivistanê derneketine, maşalla gilek paqij in.
 
Meaning winter hasn't fully emerged yet, mashallah they are
very clean.

301
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:30,000
Emê mûkê din baîv jî bixwin înşalla.
 
We will eat some almonds too, God willing.

302
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:50,000
Kakê Şivan... Şivan kotî ber pês.
 
Brother Shevan... Shevan [unclear phrase/name, possibly
"load back"].

303
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:05,000
Erê hevalê me, bîse mwa rone, ev rêka, rêka gundê Qada ye.
 
Yes our friends, please look, this road is the road to Qada
Village.

304
00:24:05,000 --> 00:24:20,000
Hember me gundê Qada ye.
 
Opposite us is Qada Village.

305
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:23,000
Zifta xwe çîçike pak e viderê.
 
Its asphalt is a bit clean here.

306
00:24:23,000 --> 00:24:33,000
Ha rêkê camaat çîçike te'ban bîne hîşta. Çend sal n zift
nebîne.
 
Look at the road folks, it is a bit tired [worn out] still.
It hasn't seen asphalt for several years.

307
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:40,000
Şebabê gundê Qada, li sêr kin. Kase nal gind, kase nal
mantiqê.
 
The youth of Qada Village, watch them. People of the
village, people of the region.

308
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:45,000
Ev gundê wa ye hîşta.
 
This is their village still.

309
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:49,000
Em dîsa war o bibên zîkrayatê wa kî di viderê pirr in.
 
We again tell you, their memories here are many.

310
00:24:49,000 --> 00:24:52,000
Viderê mel'eb çêkirine, li mel'eb jî bigirin.
 
Here they built a stadium, capture the stadium too.

311
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:58,000
Oo viderê şebabê gundê Qada, mel'eb xweş çêkirine li nav
herd.
 
Oh, here the youth of Qada Village, they made a nice stadium
in the ground.

312
00:24:58,000 --> 00:25:18,000
Welle bes têra go gukê heye, rindi kîbar e.
 
Well, but it's enough for playing ball, it's good and
decent.

313
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:28,000
Sek viderê, hîn kîlkî baîvê napaqij in.
 
Look here, still the almond shells are not clean
[unopened/unripe].

314
